# XSH getrusage()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# getrusage() is XSI. The page names only ru_utime and ru_stime as members
# of the result and says nothing about their accuracy, granularity or
# normalisation, so the tests ask only for what a measure of processor
# time must do: be positive after the process (or a waited-for child) has
# spent a good part of a second in a busy loop, and not go backwards. The
# busy loops are bounded by wall-clock time, not by the processor-time
# counters under test. Times are compared as microsecond totals of
# ru_utime and ru_stime. Not tested: other members, the contents for a
# terminated child that has not been waited for (the page does not say),
# SA_NOCLDWAIT (SIG_IGN for SIGCHLD is used for the discarded-child case).

assertion  XSH.getrusage.001
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF) returns 0; after the process has run a
           busy loop that used 300 ms of processor time (measured with clock()), the total of ru_utime
           and ru_stime is above 0 and not below the total read before the
           loop.
note       The busy loop is capped by CLOCK_MONOTONIC (5 s); a reading of zero
           after 300 ms of processor time means the measure is not one of
           processor time used.
           Q-88: accuracy and granularity are not defined; only positive and not decreasing are asked.
test       t/001-self.c

assertion  XSH.getrusage.002
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       After a child that used 300 ms of processor time in a busy loop has terminated and
           been waited for, the total of ru_utime and ru_stime from
           getrusage(RUSAGE_CHILDREN) is larger than before the child was
           created.
note       Q-88: accuracy and granularity are not defined; only positive and not decreasing are asked.
test       t/002-children.c

assertion  XSH.getrusage.003
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       RUSAGE_CHILDREN also covers the descendants of children, when
           they have terminated and been waited for: a child that waits for
           a grandchild running a busy loop (300 ms), and is itself waited
           for, leaves the total larger than before.
note       Q-88: accuracy and granularity are not defined; only positive and not decreasing are asked.
test       t/003-grandchildren.c

assertion  XSH.getrusage.004
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       A child that is never waited for (SIGCHLD set to SIG_IGN, so that
           wait() ends with ECHILD once the child is gone) is discarded: the
           two totals from getrusage(RUSAGE_CHILDREN) before the fork and
           after the wait are equal, even though the child ran a busy loop.
note       Change history: the RUSAGE_CHILDREN wording was clarified in
           Issue 8.
test       t/004-discarded-child.c

assertion  XSH.getrusage.005
anchor     functions/getrusage.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       getrusage() with a who value that is neither RUSAGE_SELF nor
           RUSAGE_CHILDREN (tried: -1, INT_MAX, INT_MIN; at least one must
           be refused) returns -1 with EINVAL for each that is refused.
note       An implementation may define more values (RUSAGE_THREAD), so a
           candidate that succeeds is skipped.
test       t/005-einval.c
